The '''Mandalorian secret covert'''<ref name="Graphic Novel">[[The Mandalorian – The Graphic Novel of Season 3|''The Mandalorian'' – The Graphic Novel of Season 3]]</ref> was a covert established by the [[Children of the Watch]] on a [[Armorer's planet|barren terrestrial planet]] within a cave system that was near a body of [[water]], after maintaining a [[Mandalorian covert]] on the [[Glavis Ringworld]]. The [[covert]] consisted of many [[Mandalorian warrior]]s, including the [[Heavy Infantry Mandalorian]] [[Paz Vizsla]], and [[Youngling|children]]. They were led by "[[The Armorer]]." During the recital of vows of the [[Mandalorian Creed]] by [[Ragnar Vizsla|Ragnar]], the covert was [[Skirmish outside a Mandalorian covert|attacked]] by a large [[Reptile|reptilian]] creature. Originally facing difficulty in defeating the beast, the covert was saved by [[Din Djarin]] in his [[Din Djarin's N-1 starfighter|modified]] [[N-1 starfighter]].<ref name="The Apostate" />

Following an [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]] [[Bombing of Kryze Castle|attack]] on Lady [[Bo-Katan Kryze]]'s [[Kryze Fortress|castle]] on [[Kalevala]], Djarin and Kryze retreated to the covert. There, Djarin presented the covert with proof that Mandalore, its mines and the Living Waters had survived the purge. Djarin and Kryze were welcomed into the covert.<ref name="Ch. 19">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 19: The Convert}}</ref>

The [[New Republic]] pilot [[Captain]] [[Carson Teva]] came to the covert that the he call the Mandalorians for help that the [[Gorian Shard's pirate crew|Pirate Nation]] led by the [[Pirate King]] [[Gorian Shard]] took over the [[Nevarro City|city]] of [[Nevarro]]. In response, the Mandalorians returned to Nevarro and defeated the pirates, earning land on the planet in the process.<ref name="The Pirate">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 21: The Pirate}}</ref>

